  "narrative": "This synthesis closes H7 and H17 as independently validated dataset associations. H7, MSI-high versus WRN dependency signed for stronger dependency, has discovery R7 signed +0.790 with 95% CI +0.760 to +0.819 and validation R93 signed +0.805 with independent CI +0.758 to +0.851 at the stricter validation alpha. The effect is far above the approximate 10% clinical threshold for WRN and excludes both null and clinically small effects under the validation interval. H17, PTEN loss versus stronger STAT3 dependency, has discovery R24 signed +0.267 with 95% CI +0.215 to +0.319 and validation R66 signed +0.307 with independent CI +0.228 to +0.387, also far above the approximate 10% threshold for STAT3. These are observational associations in the supplied lung-cell-line profiles, not causal mechanisms or externally generalizable claims. H2 is assessed as rejected for the original claim that EGFR amplification is associated with clinically meaningful stronger EGFR dependency: discovery R2 is borderline and imprecise, with a signed estimate near the threshold but an interval that includes the null, and validation R13 has a below-threshold signed estimate with an interval compatible with no meaningful effect. Current supported findings are SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency, and CDKN2A loss in TP53-wildtype cells with stronger MDM2 dependency, with the first five now independently validated and the sixth accepted on strong discovery evidence but not yet independently validated. Negative findings include lack of clinically meaningful support for overall EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, PIK3CA mutation, NF1-loss BRAF or RIT1 associations, APC mutation with TMED10, MYC amplification with POLR2A or USP7, ARID1A loss with SMARCA2, and BRAF V600E with BRAF dependency. KRAS overall and several conditional EGFR or KRAS contexts remain unresolved or failed validation. Unresolved questions include conditional EGFR in KRAS-mutant cells, research-marker TMED10 probes, MYC-high POLR2A or RPL11 effects, STK11 and TP53 co-mutation contexts, lineage heterogeneity for accepted associations, BRCA2-related DHX9 or WRN effects, and TP53-loss MDM2 complements. The most informative next analysis is independent validation of H140 in the next appraise because it is the strongest new accepted effect, CDKN2A loss in TP53-wildtype cells associated with much stronger MDM2 dependency, signed +0.119 with 95% CI +0.079 to +0.158, several times the approximate clinical threshold and large enough that multiplicity concerns are modest. After that, analyze the already registered robustness strata H143 to H146 and the TP53-loss complement H147. If validation budget remains, secondary candidates are H90, conditional EGFR in KRAS-mutant cells, or H4, overall KRAS mutation versus KRAS dependency, but H140 is the highest-value priority.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 7 synthesis. H7 MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency is now validated and closed. H17 PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency deadline closed. H2 overall EGFR amplification with stronger EGFR dependency rejected as clinically meaningful after non-decisive discovery and weak validation. Core validated associations: H5 SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, H17 PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, H73 TP53 loss with weaker USP7 dependency, H20 KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency, and H7 MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency. H140 CDKN2A loss in TP53-wildtype cells with stronger MDM2 dependency remains accepted and active as the strongest new discovery-only association, R88 signed +0.119, 95% CI +0.079 to +0.158. Next appraise priority: request validation of H140. Then analyze H143-H146 robustness strata and H147 TP53-loss complement. Secondary validation candidates: H90 EGFR amplification within KRAS-mutant cells and H4 KRAS overall. Keep conclusions observational within the supplied dataset and avoid causal or generalizability claims."
